<description>
Fill each blue rectangular frame with teal and extend teal outward from any one-cell border gap.

Input structure
- The grid has a black background and one foreground color forming 4-connected rectangular frame objects.
- Each frame's bounding-box border is either complete or has exactly one missing non-corner border pixel.
- Frame interiors and the outward line from each border gap are black in the input.
Rule
- For every frame, recolor all pixels strictly inside its bbox to teal.
- If the frame has a missing border pixel, recolor that gap and every black pixel from it straight outward, perpendicular to that side, through the grid edge.
- Keep the blue frame pixels and all other black background pixels unchanged.
Key insight
- A missing border pixel is not a defect to repair with blue; it is a doorway that defines the direction of the teal spill from the filled rectangle.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_along_path",
  "src": "blue rectangular frame objects; any one-cell non-corner missing border pixel is the ray source",
  "path": "straight outward ray perpendicular to the side containing the gap, continuing through black background to the grid edge",
  "trajectory": "paint the gap and ray pixels teal",
  "transform": "fill every blue frame's bbox interior teal and preserve the blue border pixels"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 24-26 rows x 25-28 cols, black background
  frames:
    count: 5-6 blue (color 1) rectangular frames per grid
    size: 3-8 rows x 5-9 cols (each dimension >= 3)
    structure: 1-pixel-wide border of blue; interior is black; all frame pixels lie on bbox perimeter
    gap: 0 or 1 missing non-corner border pixel per frame; ~70% of frames have a gap [observed]
    gap_position: on any of the 4 sides, not at a corner; varies across all 4 directions
    gap_side_fraction: 0.25-0.60 along the non-corner positions of the side [observed]
  placement:
    no bbox overlap between any two frames; min bbox gap >= 2 cells
    frames at least 1 cell from grid edge
  rays:
    from each gap, a straight line extends outward perpendicular to the gapped side to the grid edge
    ray must pass only through black cells (no collision with other frames)
    ray_length: 1-10 cells (gap to grid edge, exclusive of gap)
  output:
    fill each frame interior (strictly inside bbox) with teal (color 8)
    gap pixel + all ray pixels recolored teal
    blue frame border pixels preserved unchanged

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Choose grid size 24-28 x 24-28.
    2. Choose 5-6 frame bboxes (each 3-8 x 5-9); place them with >= 2 cell gap between bboxes and >= 1 cell from grid edge.
    3. For each frame, decide gap or no-gap (~70% with gap). For gapped frames, pick a side and a non-corner position on it.
    4. Validate rays: from each gap, trace outward perpendicular to the side; ensure the ray reaches the grid edge without intersecting any other frame bbox. Reject/retry placement if violated.
    5. Build input: draw blue border pixels for each frame (omitting gap pixel); everything else black.
    6. Build output: fill interiors with teal, draw gap+ray pixels as teal, keep blue borders.
```
